# env
# Broad on purpose. The live credential file for this project is
# `ulmara-fe-backend.env` -- a `*.env` name, which the three rules below did
# not cover, so it would have been tracked by default if copied in here.
# `.env.*` is here as much for backups as for originals: a stray `*.env.bak`
# holding a real key has leaked on the backend before.
# The negations must stay LAST -- gitignore is last-match-wins, so a
# `!.env.example` placed above `*.env.*` would silently do nothing.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env
*.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

# macos
.DS_Store

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# vscode
.vscode/

# logs
*.log
